1) what is Singleton class?
Ans: A class which should have Only one instance always exist at max.
Advantages:

  1) Reusability of the exiting object that save memory and time of create repeated object.
  2) Easy to implement
  3) No need to pass object to different method as it globally available.
  4)Resources like database connections, configuration settings, or caches are managed from a single place.

Disadvantages:
   1) It breaks SRP(SOLID) since pure singleton class always implement inside Business logic class. Hence every business class have by default 2 responsiblites one
      is create singleton object and another implement their own business logic.
   2) Can not do unit test for singleton class.
   3) Simple implementation of singleton class is not sufficient to prevent thread safe.
   4) Hidden global dependency that make its tightly coupled.
Where to use:
    1) Logger
    2) Configuration
    3) DB connection
    4) Utility class
    5) Session management
How to implement :

    1) static private variable
    2) private constructor
    3) static public method which return  static final objects.

  Tread safe:
     1) lazy initialization
     2) Eager initialization
     3) Double check
     4) Bill pugh
     5) synchronized


